{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,12]],"date-time":"2026-03-12T16:56:11Z","timestamp":1773334571506,"version":"3.50.1"},"reference-count":78,"publisher":"American Astronomical Society","issue":"2","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2016,5,25]],"date-time":"2016-05-25T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1464134400000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/iopscience.iop.org\/page\/copyright"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2016,5,25]],"date-time":"2016-05-25T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1464134400000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/iopscience.iop.org\/info\/page\/text-and-data-mining"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["iopscience.iop.org"],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["ApJ"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2016,6,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>ABSTRACT<\/jats:title>\n               <jats:p>In recent years, omni-present transverse waves have been observed in all layers of the solar atmosphere. Coronal loops are often modeled as a collection of individual strands in order to explain their thermal behavior and appearance. We perform three-dimensional (3D) ideal magnetohydrodynamics simulations to study the effect of a continuous small amplitude transverse footpoint driving on the internal structure of a coronal loop composed of strands. The output is also converted into synthetic images, corresponding to the AIA 171 and 193 \u00c5 passbands, using <jats:monospace>FoMo<\/jats:monospace>. We show that the multi-stranded loop ceases to exist in the traditional sense of the word, because the plasma is efficiently mixed perpendicularly to the magnetic field, with the Kelvin\u2013Helmholtz instability acting as the main mechanism. The final product of our simulation is a mixed loop with density structures on a large range of scales, resembling a power-law. Thus, multi-stranded loops are unstable to driving by transverse waves, and this raises strong doubts on the usability and applicability of coronal loop models consisting of independent strands.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.3847\/0004-637x\/823\/2\/82","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2016,5,25]],"date-time":"2016-05-25T16:13:40Z","timestamp":1464192820000},"page":"82","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1088\/crossmark-policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":41,"title":["THE INSTABILITY AND NON-EXISTENCE OF MULTI-STRANDED LOOPS WHEN DRIVEN BY TRANSVERSE WAVES"],"prefix":"10.3847","volume":"823","author":[{"given":"N.","family":"Magyar","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-9628-4113","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"T.","family":"Van Doorsselaere","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"2208","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2016,5,25]]},"reference":[{"key":"apj523515bib1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"A107","DOI":"10.1051\/0004-6361\/201322094","volume":"560","author":"Anfinogentov","year":"2013","journal-title":"A&A"},{"key":"apj523515bib2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"A136","DOI":"10.1051\/0004-6361\/201526195","volume":"583","author":"Anfinogentov","year":"2015","journal-title":"A&A"},{"key":"apj523515bib3","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"72","DOI":"10.1088\/0004-637X\/809\/1\/72","volume":"809","author":"Antolin","year":"2015","journal-title":"ApJ"},{"key":"apj523515bib4","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"152","DOI":"10.1088\/0004-637X\/745\/2\/152","volume":"745","author":"Antolin","year":"2012","journal-title":"ApJ"},{"key":"apj523515bib5","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"L22","DOI":"10.1088\/2041-8205\/787\/2\/L22","volume":"787","author":"Antolin","year":"2014","journal-title":"ApJL"},{"key":"apj523515bib6","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"1059","DOI":"10.1086\/309486","volume":"541","author":"Aschwan